Important — the API auth module differs from what I assumed in the frontend:
- `/auth/register` — POST {name, email, password, phone} → session (no OTP!)
- `/auth/login` — POST {email, password} → session
- `/auth/phone/request-otp` — POST {phone} → {message, expiresIn, devOtp}
- `/auth/phone/verify` — POST {phone, otp} → session
- `/auth/google` — POST {profile, idToken}
- `/auth/forgot-password` — POST {email} → {message, devResetUrl}
- `/auth/reset-password` — POST {token, password}
- `/auth/refresh` — POST {refreshToken} → session
- `/auth/logout` — POST {refreshToken}
- `/auth/me` — GET → {user, memberships}

So my login/signup/otp pages are wrong. Login requires email+password (no phone identifier). Signup is direct (no OTP). Let me fix the auth pages to match reality:
- LoginPage: email + password → session → /app. Also offer "Login with phone OTP" and "Mock Google".
- SignupPage: name, email, phone, password → session directly → /app. 
- OTP page: phone-based phone login.
- ForgotPassword: email → devResetUrl (link with token). ResetPassword: token + password.

Let me check the loginSchema/registerSchema in shared/schemas.ts to get exact fields.

