Two findings:

1. **Tailwind v4 `@apply btn` error**: In Tailwind v4, `@apply` of a custom class (`.btn`) defined in the same `@layer components` doesn't work — v4 requires `@utility` directive for custom utilities to be apply-able, or you just can't `@apply` arbitrary component classes. Fix: expand the `.btn-*` classes to not reference `.btn`, or convert `.btn` to a `@utility`. Simplest robust fix: inline the btn properties into each variant, or define `.btn` properties via `@utility btn { ... }` then `@apply btn`? Actually in Tailwind v4, `@apply` only works with utilities, and custom classes aren't utilities. Use `@utility btn` won't help for applying to component classes either... Actually `@utility` creates a utility that CAN be used with `@apply`. But then `.btn-primary { @apply btn ... }` — `btn` becomes a utility, so `@apply btn` works. Let me use `@utility btn { ... }` at top level (not inside a layer), then keep `.btn-primary { @apply btn ... }` in components layer.

Wait, does @utility allow `@apply` inside it? @utility can contain declarations and @apply of built-in utilities. Yes. And then `.btn-primary { @apply btn bg-saffron-600 ... }` would work since `btn` is now a registered utility.

Let me convert `.btn` to `@utility btn`. The other classes `.card`, `.input`, `.label`, `.badge` are used in markup directly as classes (not via @apply), so they're fine as component classes.

Actually simpler: I can just remove the `@apply btn` references and inline the common button properties. But that duplicates. The @utility approach is cleaner. Let me do:

```
@utility btn {
  @apply inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-xl px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold transition-all focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-saffron-400 disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed;
}
```

Hmm, but @apply inside @utility in Tailwind v4.2... I believe it's supported (nested @apply in @utility is allowed). Let me try it.

2. **Templates GET /:templateId EXISTS** — great, the editor's fetch works. Good. So my earlier concern is resolved — I misread earlier truncation.

Now verify other routes: trusts (committee, audit-log, by-code), users (/me/donations), receipts (list include donation), donations (list include receipts), reports export. Let me read those route files quickly.

